The fix for #574 is committed and queued to land, but it hasn't merged yet. The queue still hadn't reached it after about 3h20m, and the run is at its time limit. The manager will merge it after this run ends and post the verdict on the issue; the next run finishes the rest.

**What changed:** commit `5c067b2b` on `looper/tacplus-574`. sitegen now opens the repository and the docs directory once each with `os.OpenRoot`, and does every read, stat and write through them. A link or snippet path that climbs out with `..` or follows a symbolic link outside is now an error, and the file outside is not read. The same commit fixes the other three sites of this finding (#573, #575, #576). Two new tests cover a snippet marker with `../` past the root and a link that leaves through a symbolic link.

**Checks run:**
- `just docs` passes: "sitegen: the links of 45 documents resolve", "no leaks found", and `ok cmd/sitegen` in the test step.
- gosec reports no G703 in `cmd/sitegen/`. It still reports one MEDIUM finding (G304) at `cmd/sitegen/annotations.go:107`, on a file protoc writes to a temporary location; that predates this change and is outside the issue.
- The full `just gates` locally ran about 3h20m with no FAIL, but I stopped it at the run's limit before it finished. The land will run the full gates anyway, because the change is under `cmd/`.
- The trace check found nothing in sitegen, which has no service handlers. Its only findings are in `cross-test/server-runtime/client/go/main.go`, which this change doesn't touch, and they're already filed as #311.

**Backports:** the pull requests #593–#598 (release/2.1 through release/2.6) are open, mergeable and green. release/2.0 has no sitegen, so it needs none. I won't tag `v2.6.2` on main, because main has taken features since `v2.6.1`. The patch ships as the next `v2.6.x` on release/2.6 once #598 merges.

**Left for the next run:** confirm the land verdict, add main's commit hash to the bodies of #593–#598, comment on #574 (and on #573, #575, #576), then close the issue. All of this is in the last checkpoint.
